This is your first post. Edit it, rename the directory to a real slug,
or delete it entirely. Posts live in `content/posts/<slug>/index.md`
with sibling asset files (images, etc.) next to them — Abqari's
bundle convention lets you reference `hero.jpg` in this post body and
the image pipeline rewrites it into a responsive `<picture>` block
on build.

## How to write posts

```bash
bin/new post "My next post"   # scaffolds content/posts/<date>-my-next-post/index.md
```

Drop colocated images in the bundle directory and reference them by
relative path:

```markdown
![A hero image](hero.jpg)
```

The image pipeline takes care of AVIF + WebP variants, multiple
widths, and the correct `<source>` order. The `<img>` keeps its
`width` and `height` attributes so there's no layout shift.

## Posts you'll see surfaced

On a single post page, the engine renders three optional tail
sections (toggle each under `posts.show:` in `config/site.yml`):

- **Table of contents** — built from h2/h3 headings when there are
  three or more
- **Up next** — single card linking to the next chronological post
- **Related** — grid of posts sharing tags (or whatever `match_by:`
  field you point it at)

Each is silent when there's nothing meaningful to show.

## Configuration

Toggle the collections and modules you need in `config/site.yml`.
The defaults give you `posts` only; flip on `photos`, `publications`,
or `workshops` when you have content for them.
